### Issues

#### CRITICAL

| ID | Severity | Description |
|----|----------|-------------|
| **CRIT-01** | **CRITICAL** | **WS router mounted at wrong prefix**. `main.py:141` reads `app.include_router(ws_router, tags=["ws"])` — missing `prefix="/api/v1"`. Frontend connects to `/api/v1/ws` (line 39 of `useLiveMetrics.ts`), but backend serves WS at `/ws`. The WS connection will fail, realtime updates won't work (polling fallback is the only working path). **Fix**: change line 141 to `app.include_router(ws_router, prefix="/api/v1", tags=["ws"])`. |
| **CRIT-02** | **CRITICAL** | **TypeScript compilation fails**. `src/tests/setup.ts:14:3` — `TS2741: Property 'fromRect' is missing in type 'typeof DOMRect'`. The mock class declared at line 14 lacks the `fromRect` static method from the `DOMRect` DOM type (available in TS 5.7+ with `lib: ["DOM"]`). Frontend build (`tsc -b`) will fail. **Fix**: add `static fromRect() { return new DOMRect() }` inside the mock class. |

#### WARNING

| ID | Severity | Description |
|----|----------|-------------|
| WARN-01 | WARNING | **CORS_ORIGINS defaults to empty string**. `config.py:16` sets `CORS_ORIGINS: str = ""`, so the middleware is added but with empty origins. Vite proxy avoids this in dev, but anyone connecting from a different port without proxy will hit CORS blocks. Acknowledged in design as deferred to Fase 8 (nginx). |
| WARN-02 | WARNING | **Login password validation uses min(1)**. `LoginPage.tsx:12`: `z.string().min(1, 'Password is required')`. Register uses `min(8)`. Login intentionally allows any non-empty password since it's just authentication — the backend handles password rejection. Not a bug, just a UX inconsistency. |

